# EMULATOR ONLY. Mac build first runs ChatScreenRenderTest, whose parsed HTTP409
# fixture is chat/build/render/mac-refusal.json. Push it to /data/local/tmp/mac-refusal.json.
# Back up emulator files/oma-chat.json before this walk and restore it afterward.
# No runner key or real session is needed; network parsing/persistence is covered by MacThreadsTest.
# As root, in one step with the stop: the home app restarts at once after a force-stop.
shell 'am force-stop dev.omalauncher.boss; d=/data/data/dev.omalauncher.boss; cp /data/local/tmp/mac-refusal.json $d/files/oma-chat.json && chown $(stat -c %u:%g $d) $d/files/oma-chat.json && restorecon $d/files/oma-chat.json'
fold folded
launch dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.oma.OmaChatActivity
expect Continue the project
expect This Claude conversation is still open on the Mac.
expect Close that conversation there before replying from the phone.
expect No phone turn was started.
absent The Mac could not take this (HTTP 409).
shot mac-refusal-cover
fold open
expect Close that conversation there before replying from the phone.
shot mac-refusal-inner
[phone] After promotion, try a harmless reply to a held-open spare Mac conversation: the inline explanation must appear beneath the preserved prompt, not only HTTP409. Verify no remote turn is queued.
[phone] Close the spare on the Mac, retry the prompt from Soma and verify one real reply in that same session.
